meta {
  name: Overage - Get
  type: http
  seq: 17
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/workspaces/:workspace/billing/overage
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  workspace: {{workspaceId}}
}

docs {
  The workspace's credit overage settings — whether it keeps running once its
  plan allowance and top-up pool are both spent, and what that is allowed to
  cost. Requires the `billing.view` permission.

  - `available` — whether the current plan sells overage (the
    `credit_overage` feature). `false` on the Free plan.
  - `enabled` — whether the workspace opted in.
  - `limit` — the cap the workspace chose, or `null` for "use the default".
  - `effective_limit` — the cap actually enforced this period. `null` means
    uncapped, which only happens when the estate default is uncapped.
  - `maximum_limit` — the highest cap the workspace may set
    (`config('billing.overage.default_limit')`, 1,000,000 by default).
  - `credits_used` / `credits_remaining` — overage spent and still available
    in the current billing period. `credits_remaining` is `0` whenever
    overage is unavailable or switched off, and `null` when uncapped.
  - `credit_value_usd` — what each overage credit will be billed at.

  Response is wrapped: `{ success, statusCode, message, data: { overage } }`.
}
